From c981c0a607be2716759524dbe9c432d7b6e95508 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Den Zuko <denzuko@dapla.net>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:28:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH consfigurator] doc: note libacl1-dev/libcap-dev build
 dependency

Loading Consfigurator outside of the packaged .deb -- via Quicklisp or
straight from git -- fails partway through the build with a
CFFI-GROVEL:GROVEL-ERROR on src/libacl.lisp (sys/acl.h) and then again
on src/libcap.lisp (sys/capability.h) once the first is resolved,
since neither header ships by default on a minimal system and the two
failures surface one at a time rather than together.

Installation.rst covers the Debian/derivative and Quicklisp/git paths
but doesn't mention either header is needed, which cost an hour of
apt-get whack-a-mole to track down from the outside. Adding a short
note with the two package names for Debian/Ubuntu.
---
 doc/installation.rst | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/installation.rst b/doc/installation.rst
index a1eef8b..4316116 100644
--- a/doc/installation.rst
+++ b/doc/installation.rst
@@ -32,3 +32,21 @@ If you would like to follow development more closely, you can::
     % git clone https://git.spwhitton.name/consfigurator ~/.local/share/common-lisp/source/consfigurator
 
 and ASDF should pick it up.
+
+Native library dependencies
+----------------------------
+
+Loading Consfigurator groveled bindings against two POSIX headers that
+aren't always present outside of a Debian/derivative environment where
+the packaged ``.deb`` pulls in its own build dependencies:
+``sys/acl.h`` (``src/libacl.lisp``, from ``libacl1-dev`` on
+Debian/Ubuntu) and ``sys/capability.h`` (``src/libcap.lisp``, from
+``libcap-dev``). On a system installing Consfigurator via Quicklisp or
+straight from git rather than the ``.deb``, both headers need to be
+installed first, or ``asdf:load-system`` fails with a
+``CFFI-GROVEL:GROVEL-ERROR`` partway through the build — first on
+``libacl``, and then again on ``libcap`` once ``libacl1-dev`` is
+installed, since the two failures don't surface at the same time. On
+Debian/Ubuntu::
+
+    % apt-get install libacl1-dev libcap-dev
-- 
